From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:10:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the broadcast exchange's assert-only check only when asserts are on

Assert-only code in pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp binds the outcome
of an insertion that only D_ASSERT() reads, so in a release build,
where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the binding is set and never used
and -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. The assert-only lines are
compiled only when assertions are enabled, with the insertion kept in
both builds, which is the shape upstream gives the site later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp
index ea98aed70d..e522e27356 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp
@@ -1351,8 +1351,12 @@ SourceResultType PipelineBroadcastExchange::ReserveScanLocked(
 		auto position = consumer.position++;
 		buffer->ReserveRead(position, scan_state.spool_reader, next_chunk, batch_index, spool_read);
 		if (spool_read.IsSet()) {
+#ifdef D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
 			auto inserted = consumer.in_flight_reads.insert(position);
 			D_ASSERT(inserted.second);
+#else
+			consumer.in_flight_reads.insert(position);
+#endif
 		} else {
 			consumer.rows_read += next_chunk->size();
 			RetireChunksLocked();
